//? Title: Range coding: actual integer intervals, emitted bytes and static-model cost
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Entropy coding assigns shorter descriptions to more probable symbols while
preserving an exact decode under a shared model. The native carry-free range
coder narrows32-bit intervals and emits settled bytes as it renormalizes. Actual
register and byte histories now support the explanation. The original
50:20:20:10 model and twelve repeated-pattern sizes remain, with explicit
framing, model and truncation controls.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Let F be the positive model total and C_s its cumulative prefix. The producer
computes u=floor(R/F), then updates
$$ L\gets L+C_su\pmod{2^{32}},\qquad R\gets f_su. $$
\alttext(The actual integer range narrows by the symbol cumulative count and frequency.)
Models have total at most65536, matching the minimum normalized range and
preventing a zero subdivision unit. Byte renormalization follows the actual
top-byte or bottom-range correction branch, shifting low and range by eight
bits; decoding makes the same subdivisions while shifting in real bytes. A final
four-byte low flush initializes the decoder code register.

The ideal static-model cost is \(-\sum_s n_s\log_2(f_s/F)\), plus finite
precision/framing overhead. With matching empirical proportions this gives the
entropy reference, not a claim that every finite output equals entropy. The byte
stream alone contains neither the model nor the symbol count. The original
message is a deterministic ordered repetition, not an iid draw; the measured
cost is still a real code length for that known static model.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/range_coding_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = a::range_encode_trace({0, 1}, {1, 1});
    auto decoded = a::range_decode_trace(t.bytes, {1, 1}, 2);
    const auto &s = t.steps[0];
    std::print("\n| actual symbol | low before | range before | actual unit | actual narrowed low | actual " "narrowed range | byte shifts |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.symbol,
                   e.low_before, e.range_before, e.unit, e.low_narrowed,
                   e.range_narrowed, e.shifts.size());
    std::print("Actual decoded values: {}.\n", decoded.symbols);

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first subdivision unit\n{}", s.unit));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual first narrowed interval\nlow {}, range {}",
                       s.low_narrowed, s.range_narrowed));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0},
           std::format("Actual flushed bytes / decoded count\n{} / {}",
                       t.bytes.size(), decoded.symbols.size()));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/range_coding_tiny.svg");
}
```
